#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, you'll build a minimal Go tool that authenticates a user with [atproto OAuth](/guides/auth) and fetches their session info. The entire app fits in a single file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a good starting point for understanding how OAuth works in AT Protocol. For a TypeScript version, see the [OAuth with Node Tutorial](/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial). For building production web apps, see the [OAuth with NextJS Tutorial](/guides/oauth-tutorial).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "You should have a working understanding of Go.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should have installed:\n"
"- Go 1.24+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:32
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "You should also have an atproto handle to test with.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a new Go module and install the [Go SDK](https://github.com/bluesky-social/indigo):\n"
msgstr ""

