#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "That's it — the Go SDK includes everything you need for OAuth, including an in-memory session store for development.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:42
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 2: Build the OAuth Client\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create `main.go`. Start with the imports and the OAuth client setup:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now add the `run` function. First, set up a callback server on a random port, then configure the OAuth client:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NewLocalhostConfig` sets up a loopback client.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:56
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"OAuth loopback works by using a special redirect URI (like `http://127.0.0.1:PORT/callback`) to send authorization codes directly back to an app, which listens on a local port, avoiding browser-based callbacks and enabling secure, direct communication for token exchange. Instead of a web redirect, the app opens a local listener, you can auth in a browser, and the server redirects back to the app's local URI, letting the app grab the code and exchange it for a token. It's particularly useful for development scenarios.\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NewMemStore` provides in-memory session storage for development.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:60
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 3: Login Flow\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Continue the `run` function with the login flow. This resolves the handle, opens the browser, and waits for the callback:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:66
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "The flow works like this:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. `StartAuthFlow` resolves the user's handle, discovers their PDS, sends a [Pushed Authorization Request (PAR)](/guides/permission-sets#requesting-permissions), and returns an authorization URL.\n"
"2. The user's browser opens to a consent screen.\n"
"3. After the user approves, their PDS redirects back to `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/callback` with an authorization code.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:72
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 4: Use the Session\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complete the `run` function by exchanging the callback for a session and making an authenticated API call:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ProcessCallback` exchanges the authorization code for tokens. `ResumeSession` wraps those tokens in a session that handles DPoP signing and token refresh automatically. `APIClient()` returns an HTTP client pre-configured with the user's credentials — you can use it to make any [XRPC](/specs/xrpc) call.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 5: Helper Functions\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add the callback server and browser-opening helpers:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "The callback server listens on `127.0.0.1:0`, which tells the OS to assign any available port. When the callback arrives, it sends the query parameters through a channel back to the main flow and shuts itself down.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 6: Run It\n"
msgstr ""

